new('REQ-807','Which items a team re-orders','PH-10b',['Q-REORDER'],
 '`queue.reorder_scope`: `all` (default) or `command_team`. With `command_team` a rank change (`--priority`, `--replan`) and a re-densify by a `backlog team` command re-order only the items bound to the command team; other items keep their positions (template `command_team` = today, R1-007).',
 'R1-007: the seam `inScope` limited the re-order to the session team without a key.',
 ['With `command_team`, `team update 3 --priority 0` of t1 moves item 3 before t1\'s other items and leaves item 2 of team t2 at its index position.','With `all`, the same command re-densifies every item.'],
 [('a team re-orders only its own items',BG_TEAM+'\n  And I run `backlog new --name x`\n  And I run `backlog team new --team t1 --agent lead --name a`\nWhen I run `backlog team update 2 --team t1 --agent lead --priority 0`\nThen the command succeeds\n  And I run `backlog list --json`\n  And the output contains "x"'),
  ('with reorder_scope all every item is re-ordered','Given a repository with a backlog\n  And the backlog registers the workflow "team" from the template "team.full.json" with `queue.reorder_scope = "all"`\n  And a team "t1" with lead "lead" and members "ann, bob" using the workflow "team"\n  And I run `backlog new --name x`\n  And I run `backlog team new --team t1 --agent lead --name a`\nWhen I run `backlog team update 2 --team t1 --agent lead --priority 0`\nThen the command succeeds')],
 [('engine-queue.test.js','reorder_scope command_team vs all','home with items of t1, t2 and outside a team','index order: only t1 items move (command_team); every item re-densified (all)')],'team-queue')
